<title>NETHERLANDS: BOSCH &amp; KEUNING SLIPS TO FIRST-HALF LOSS.</title>
<headline>BOSCH &amp; KEUNING SLIPS TO FIRST-HALF LOSS.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM, Netherlands 1996-09-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>First-half 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of guilders unless otherwise stated)</p>
<p>    Net loss				 1.4  vs   1.1 profit</p>
<p>    Turnover				49.6  vs  46.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax loss			   2.1  vs   1.7 profit</p>
<p>NOTES - Bosch &amp; Keuning NV said the first-half loss was</p>
<p>largely the result of a change in seasonal business patterns as</p>
<p>a result of the acquisition of Nijgh &amp; Van Ditmar Educatief.</p>
<p>It said that for the whole of 1996 it was sticking to its</p>
<p>previous forecast that full-year results would be comparable</p>
<p>with the previous year.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
